{"id":"446944151","kind":"article","title":"写你所读，以求内化","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zg3fYweZpbHeBTpcYke5mF4ZfrJutYcQEtFo"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"常青笔记 & 知识工作","date":"2021-12-18","updated":"2023-01-14","votes":49,"comment_count":1,"minutes":3,"chars":1418,"keywords":["常青笔记","阅读笔记","知识管理","写作","自主思考"],"summary":"Andy Matuschak 分享个人经验，认为围绕阅读内容写作能迫使读者综合、联系并深入思考，常青笔记则可让阅读成果逐渐积累。他建议交替收集有趣片段与想法、加工为经久耐用的笔记，同时提醒这种做法未必适合每次阅读；自己需要笔记支持，也承认一些高效读者不做笔记。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/446944151","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"方法"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"参考文献"},{"id":"sec-3","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-4","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"33lflJlm\">如果你想深刻内化你所读的内容，我所知的最好方法就是围绕它们写点什么：</p><ul><li data-pid=\"mzzZABGZ\"> 因为<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zX1WtJ4ouE8sjN1NgWHsGVg8ZnVfp5Kz74Vs\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">理解概念需与其尽力较量</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"juCXwFMU\"> 具体到写作上，<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z8q1K5a8i95qARkpFwS45qqtQzM8th82TkeUg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">写作促使人们更加深入地理解</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup><br/><br/> </li><li data-pid=\"Hqrp5nKH\"> 记住：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z8QSUyNdq3CMK79KSnCW7QTR1MPHEFi4Q2LY8\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">收集材料的作用在感觉上被夸大了</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"Pi0kpOba\"> 否则你就不会<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4enRPbLXdD8X8hCfVjaRkcGkronvhcfrgSQw\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">自主思考</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li><li data-pid=\"Bbsp3_Ji\"> 因为<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6UDDkom8Aifg6mLdjT1sPtbMBweCmpyTwmJT\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">知识工作应能聚沙成塔</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup>和<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6M8kex6kDF2FT6MWqAMDQddsqUr8sphLmyy1\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">常青笔记有助于积累阅读成果</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li><li data-pid=\"eSk4zXut\"> 诚然：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z432siNjuY9G8bTsnSugyHPB1YoZWgup6eMB3\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">多数人的阅读成效不大</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-7\"><a href=\"#ref-7\">[7]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li></ul><p data-pid=\"LK1C6m_0\">对于理解深刻来说，仅仅在书本上划出重点或写上旁注是不够的：没有太多的压力去综合、联系，或去探究事物的核心。而且随着时间的推移，随着你读得越多，这些内容也不会逐步积累。而在阅读时写下<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4SDCZQeRo4xFEQ8H4qrSqd68ucpgE6LU155C\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">常青笔记</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-8\"><a href=\"#ref-8\">[8]</a></sup>则与之不同。</p><p data-pid=\"7DoDBBMp\">但当然，这种阅读方式有时候并没有意义：很多时候，你并不是真的想把深入内化文本，而且它也不一定值得耗费心力：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6e3AFda6oSsusEmf8vWevMaNLggQ9bCEgFkf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">最好的阅读方式是高度语境化的</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-9\"><a href=\"#ref-9\">[9]</a></sup>。</p><p data-pid=\"Z1fS444S\">另外值得注意的一点是：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6GNVv6RyFDewy11ZgXzce8agWxSLwJ6Ub5Rw\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">我所认识的高效阅读者和思想家在阅读时不做笔记</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-10\"><a href=\"#ref-10\">[10]</a></sup>。但至少就我个人经验而言，我自己是需要更多的支持，来有效地体会我所阅读的内容的。</p><h2 id=\"sec-1\">方法</h2><p data-pid=\"RmcYeUgS\">我们的大方针是交替地循环：</p><ol><li data-pid=\"RVeuLQ-N\"><b>收集</b>看起来有趣的段落和阅读时出现的想法：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z71FeBJGqZdyA78UNTwXCWcMGUVCWk1XsLvPS\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">如何在阅读时整理所得</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-11\"><a href=\"#ref-11\">[11]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li><li data-pid=\"0uBx2WCV\"><b>加工</b>将这些段落和思想群，写出经久耐用的笔记：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z2PJ51tCXuPFxnfFVUxxgwjvZ1geu4YnYm7hK\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">如何将阅读标注处理成常青笔记</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-12\"><a href=\"#ref-12\">[12]</a></sup><br/> </li></ol><hr/><h2 id=\"sec-2\">参考文献</h2><p data-pid=\"KPoKPOVi\">Luhmann, N. (1992). Communicating with Slip Boxes. In A. Kieserling (Ed.), &amp; M. Kuehn (Trans.), <i>Universität als Milieu: Kleine Schriften</i> (pp. 53–61). Retrieved from <a class=\"external\" href=\"http://luhmann.surge.sh/communicating-with-slip-boxes\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">http://</span><span class=\"visible\">luhmann.surge.sh/commun</span><span class=\"invisible\">icating-with-slip-boxes</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a></p><blockquote data-pid=\"S1_2mii_\">不写作就不可能思考，至少不能复杂地、网络化(<i>anschlußfähig</i>)地思考。</blockquote><p data-pid=\"vSaJRKyf\">Levy, N. (2013). Neuroethics and the Extended Mind. In J. Illes &amp; B. J. Sahakian (Eds.), <i>Oxford Handbook of Neuroethics</i> (pp. 285–294). Oxford University Press.</p><blockquote data-pid=\"YXB6deFb\">纸质笔记，或电脑屏幕上的笔记......并没有使当代物理学或其他种类的智力行为<b>容易</b>，而是使之<b>可能</b>。</blockquote><h2 id=\"sec-3\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"n6or1P6m\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"440328209\" href=\"#/post/440328209\">为有潜在价值的参考引用建立一个阅读收件箱</a></li><li data-pid=\"3PRoFv1A\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"416319260\" href=\"#/post/416319260\">常青笔记 (Evergreen notes)</a></li><li data-pid=\"nXvku4DL\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"436335609\" href=\"#/post/436335609\">常青笔记和 Zettelkasten 卡片系统的异同点</a></li><li data-pid=\"zAWw6HCj\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"438871051\" href=\"#/post/438871051\">自主思考</a></li><li data-pid=\"-5AHcvWp\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"444601013\" href=\"#/post/444601013\">用手机来收集和分流，而不是（通常）用来阅读</a></li><li data-pid=\"EHGP3umy\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"428442216\" href=\"#/post/428442216\">对笔记写作大谈特谈的人很少有严肃的使用场景</a></li><li data-pid=\"kxj3Bdfp\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"427953380\" href=\"#/post/427953380\">我的晨间写作</a></li><li data-pid=\"62XqkYCj\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"437939919\" href=\"#/post/437939919\">收集材料的作用在感觉上被夸大了</a></li><li data-pid=\"9hMHtSnw\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"450623752\" href=\"#/post/450623752\">常青笔记有助于积累阅读成果</a></li><li data-pid=\"0GjH_eE4\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"451268598\" href=\"#/post/451268598\">如何将阅读标注处理成常青笔记</a></li><li data-pid=\"vJdgr62X\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"453852965\" href=\"#/post/453852965\">我所认识的高效阅读者和思想家在阅读时不做笔记</a></li><li data-pid=\"NFa0Uaq_\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"460888905\" href=\"#/post/460888905\">如何在阅读时整理所得</a></li><li data-pid=\"31tMHrzL\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"481236886\" href=\"#/post/481236886\">最好的阅读方式是高度语境化的</a></li><li data-pid=\"m-pXk3YT\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"516086237\" href=\"#/post/516086237\">使用笔记在内容中建立联系的优缺点</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-4\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"Q85we5fr\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"5gzykm4W\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zg3fYweZpbHeBTpcYke5mF4ZfrJutYcQEtFo\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Write about what you read to internalize texts deeply (andymatuschak.org)</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 理解概念需与其尽力较量 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"442692019\" href=\"#/post/442692019\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 写作促使人们更加深入地理解 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"599025916\" href=\"#/post/599025916\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 收集材料的作用在感觉上被夸大了 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"437939919\" href=\"#/post/437939919\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 自主思考 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"438871051\" href=\"#/post/438871051\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 知识工作应能聚沙成塔 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"422894427\" href=\"#/post/422894427\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-6\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-6\">↩</a> 常青笔记有助于积累阅读成果 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"450623752\" href=\"#/post/450623752\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-7\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-7\">↩</a> 多数人的阅读成效不大 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"451515311\" href=\"#/post/451515311\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-8\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-8\">↩</a> 常青笔记 (Evergreen notes) <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"416319260\" href=\"#/post/416319260\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-9\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-9\">↩</a> 最好的阅读方式是高度语境化的 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"481236886\" href=\"#/post/481236886\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-10\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-10\">↩</a> 我所认识的高效阅读者和思想家在阅读时不做笔记 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"453852965\" href=\"#/post/453852965\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-11\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-11\">↩</a> 如何在阅读时整理所得 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"460888905\" href=\"#/post/460888905\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-12\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-12\">↩</a> 如何将阅读标注处理成常青笔记 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"451268598\" href=\"#/post/451268598\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"446450875","title":"在写作时创建推测性大纲","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":10,"minutes":4,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 常青笔记 & 知识工作"},{"id":"447217141","title":"让思想和信念有机地涌现","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":21,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 常青笔记 & 知识工作"},{"id":"440328209","title":"为有潜在价值的参考引用建立一个阅读收件箱","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":22,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"516086237","title":"使用笔记在内容中建立联系的优缺点","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":11,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"599025916","title":"写作促使人们更加深入地理解","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":19,"minutes":4,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[],"rec_answers":[{"id":"2772990761","title":"如何构建自己的笔记系统？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":755,"minutes":20,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 755 赞同","evidence":"回答以锚文本「写你所读，以求内化」直接指向目标译文；该锚文本是可辨认的标题或主题词。"},{"id":"2832363029","title":"干货答案只收藏不看是什么样的心理？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":176,"minutes":3,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 176 赞同","evidence":"逐对核对了正文的原生引文/卡片锚和目标译文标题；仅标题或关键词指向，计 1 级。"},{"id":"2831205170","title":"记笔记真的有用吗？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":174,"minutes":5,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 174 赞同","evidence":"回答以目标译文的准确标题/关键词建立链接，证据只支持标题或关键词指向。"},{"id":"2833583714","title":"如何改变『只收藏不阅读』的习惯，将各种方面知识能化为己有？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":140,"minutes":2,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 140 赞同","evidence":"回答通过明确的译文题名/术语锚点“写你所读，以求内化”指向目标页；该处与目标摘要内容相符。"},{"id":"2639109226","title":"在校本科生该怎么发表论文？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":74,"minutes":5,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 74 赞同","evidence":"回答正文含明确指向该译文的知乎内链/链接卡，按直接提及记为1级。"}]}